Bump pageant from 0.2.4 to 0.2.5 (security fix).

pageant <= 0.2.4 buffers a peer-claimed frame length of up to ~4 GiB before checking it
(GHSA-662x-8wvj-2276, low). russh depends on pageant only under cfg(windows) and Litterbox is
built for Linux, so the crate is never compiled here; the bump clears the advisory and keeps the
scanners quiet.

Lockfile only: 0.2.5 has the same dependencies as 0.2.4 and stays within russh's ^0.2, so only
its version and checksum change. Applies after litterbox-russh-0.65.1. Drop this patch once
upstream ships a release with pageant >= 0.2.5.

diff --git a/litterbox/Cargo.lock b/litterbox/Cargo.lock
--- a/litterbox/Cargo.lock
+++ b/litterbox/Cargo.lock
@@ -3526,9 +3526,9 @@
 
 [[package]]
 name = "pageant"
-version = "0.2.4"
+version = "0.2.5"
 source = "registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"
-checksum = "f0786409b5aaa884655c9b4065681db0835db0cc185a6fb19fb17a5d38656866"
+checksum = "e0bc922d9aa8cfcf598de27b3c6122cb2eeda9d6fe71527a22ebcb7f633540ff"
 dependencies = [
  "base16ct",
  "byteorder",
